#' Discharge Monitoring Report Custom Search Facility Loadings Service
#' 
#' @noMd
#' @param output Output Format Flag.  Enter one of the following keywords:
#' - JSON = Data model formatted as Javascript Object Notation (default).
#' - XML = Data model formatted as Extensible Markup Language.
#' - CSV = Results formatted as comma delimited file download.
#' @param p_cas Chemical Abstracts Service (CAS) Registry Number.
#' @param p_cerclis CERCLIS Flag. A Y value will limit results to abandoned, inactive, or uncontrolled hazardous waste sites. 
#' @param p_co Facility County Filter. Provide a single county name in combination with a state value provided via p_st.
#' @param p_cso_outfalls CSO Outfall Flag. A Y value will limit results to facilities with one or more CSO outfalls. Can only be used if p_fac_type=POTW.
#' @param p_ct Facility City Filter. Enter a single case-insensitive city name to filter results.
#' @param p_dmr_tri_link DMR facility links to TRI ID Flag. Provide a Y or N to restrict results to DMR facilities that do or do not link to TRI ID(s).
#' @param p_end_date Monitoring Period End Date. Provide a date value in MM/YYYY format to specify the last monitoring period to include in results. Parameter p_start_date must also be populated when using this parameter.
#' @param p_esa ESA-listed species flag. Provide Y or N to restrict results to DMR facilities that do or do not discharge to counties w/ ESA-listed species
#' @param p_est Estimation Function Flag. A Y value will estimates loads when monitoring data are not reported for one or more monitoring periods in a reporting year. If not specified, defaults to Y.
#' @param p_exceed Effluent limit exceedance flag. Provide Y or N to restrict results to DMR facilities with or with no effluent limit exceedances
#' @param p_fac_type Facility Type. Provide a coded value to filter on a facility type.
#' - POTW = Publicly Owned Treatment Works
#' - NON-POTW = Industrial Point Sources (non-POTW)
#' - FEDERAL = Federal facilities
#' - STATE = State facilities
#' @param p_fifra FIFRA Flag. A Y value will limit results to pesticide-producing establishments regulated under FIFRA.
#' @param p_fname Facility Name Filter. Enter a full or partial facility name to restrict results. 
#' @param p_huc 2-, 4-, 6-, or 8-character watershed code. May contain multiple comma-separated values.
#' @param p_huc_region HUC Region. 2-digit Hydrologic Unit Code
#' @param p_imp_poll Discharge pollutants contributing to impairment flag. Provide Y or N to restrict results to DMR facilities that discharge pollutants contributing to a waterbody impairment
#' @param p_imp_water Discharge to impaired waterbodies flag. Provide Y or N to restrict results to DMR facilities that discharge to impaired waterbodies.
#' @param p_intermittent_disch Intermittent Discharges Flag. A Y value will limit results to facilities with intermittent discharges.
#' @param p_lat Latitude location in decimal degrees.
#' @param p_lbs_exceed Limit results to facilities based on a specific amount (in lb) of exceedances of NPDES permit limits. Provide when p_exceed=Y is used. Cannot be combined with p_pct_exceed.
#' @param p_loads_data Loading Calculations Option. Provide a coded value to indicate the data to be used for loading calculations.
#' - DMR = DMR data only (default)
#' - PERMITONLY = Permit limits only
#' - PERMITDMR = Use permit limits for months where DMR data are missing
#' @param p_long Longitude location in decimal degrees.
#' @param p_maj Major Facility Flag.  Enter Y to restrict results to Major facilities only.
#' @param p_maj_model Major Model Basin. If results are limited to facilities that contribute to the Chesapeake Bay TMDL (p_tmdl=Y), provide a coded value for a Chesapeake Bay water basin as constructed by modeling software.
#' JAMES RIVER
#' MD EASTERN SHORE
#' PATUXENT RIVER
#' POTOMAC RIVER
#' RAPPAHANNOCK RIVER
#' SUSQUEHANNA RIVER
#' VA EASTERN SHORE
#' YORK RIVER
#' @param p_mon_loc Monitoring Location Code.
#' @param p_naics North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) Filter. Enter two to six digits to filter results to facilities having matching NAICS codes. Digits less than six will match to all codes beginning with the provided values.
#' @param p_naics2 North American Industry Classification System Filter. Enter two digit code to filter results to facilities having matching NAICS codes.  A final wild-card is always present allowing "22" to match all NAICS codes beginning with 22. 
#' @param p_nd Annual Load Calculation Option. Provide a coded value to calculate annual loads using one of three methods: 
#' - ZERO = Set all non-detects to zero
#' - HALF = Set all non-detects to ½ the detection limit
#' - LIMIT = Set all non-detects to the detection limit
#' @param p_nutrient_agg Nutrient Aggregation Option. A Y value applies a nutrient aggregation methodology to generate nitrogen and phosphorus pollutant category loads. If not specified, defaults to N.
#' @param p_owop Owner/Operator code filter. Enter one of the following values.
#' 
#' Federal = Federal facilities regulated under the NPDES program.
#' POTW = Publicly owned treatment works. Treatment works that are owned by a State, Tribe, or municipality.
#' Non-POTW = Non-publicly owned treatment works. Often referred to as "non-municipals" or "industrials".
#' 
#' @param p_param_code Five-digit numeric code identifying the parameter. See Parameter Lookup documentation for a complete list of codes.
#' @param p_param_group Parameter Grouping Option. A Y value applies a parameter grouping function to avoid double-counting loads for pollutant parameters that represent the same pollutant. If not specified, defaults to N.
#' @param p_pct_exceed Limit results to facilities based on a specific percentage of exceedances of NPDES permit limits. Provide when p_exceed=Y is used. Cannot be combined with p_lbs_exceed.
#' @param p_pct_limit_disch Specify the percentage of the permit limit that the Loading Tool should assume is actually discharged for its loading calculations. Permitted only when p_loads_data=PERMITONLY or PERMITDMR.
#' @param p_permit_id Facility identifier from one of the following EPA facility systems: National Pollutant Discharge Elimination System (NPDES) ID, Facility Registry Service (FRS) ID, Toxics Release Inventory (TRI) ID, or Clean Watersheds Needs Survey (CWNS) ID.
#' @param p_permit_type Permit classification in ICIS-NPDES. Provide a coded value.
#' - NPD = NPDES Individual Permit
#' - NGP = NPDES Master General Permit
#' - GPC = General Permit Covered Facility
#' @param p_pf_id Permit Feature ID (outfall/pipe number)
#' @param p_poll_cat Pollutant Category. Provide a keyword to limit results.
#' - NutN = Nitrogen
#' - NutP = Phosphorus
#' - ORG = Organic Enrichment
#' - SS = Solids
#' - MET = Metals
#' - PP = Clean Water Act Priority Pollutants
#' - CER = CERCLA Hazardous Substances
#' - TRI = TRI Chemicals
#' - RAD = Radionuclides 
#' - PAT = Pathogen Indicators
#' - Temp = Temperature
#' - WW = Wastewater Flow
#' - GRAD = General Radioactivity
#' - CLR = Color
#' - WET = Whole Effluent Toxicity
#' - PFAS = Per- and Polyfluoroalkyl Substances (PFAS)
#' @param p_poll_name Pollutant Name. Provide a single pollutant name to restrict results.
#' @param p_potw Publicly-Owned Treatment Works (POTW) Flag. Provide Y to restrict results to POTWs.
#' @param p_psc EPA Effluent Guidelines Point Source Category.
#' @param p_ptreatment Pretreatment Program. A Y value limits results to facilities with an approved pretreatment program. Parameter can only be passed if p_fac_type=POTW.
#' @param p_qc_flag QC Flag. A Y value limits results to loads that have been flagged as potential outliers or data errors.
#' @param p_radius Spatial Search Radius.  Enter a radius up to 100 miles in which to spatially search for facilities.
#' @param p_reg EPA Region Filter. Provide a single value of 01 through 10 to restrict results to a single EPA region.
#' @param p_sic Standard Industrial Classification (SIC) Code Filter. Enter a single 4-digit SIC Code to filter results. If more complex filtering is required, use p_sic2 and p_sic4.
#' @param p_sic2 Standard Industrial Classification (SIC) Code Filter Alternate 2. Enter a wild-card search against SIC codes.  A final wild-card is always present allowing "22" to match all SIC codes beginning with 22.  Use the "\%" character within strings to match any SIC values with the pattern.  For example, "2\%21" matches 2021, 2121, 2221, etc.
#' @param p_sig_flag Significant Discharge Facility Flag. Provide a coded value that will limits results to facilities that are or are not defined as a significant discharge facility by the jurisdiction in which they are permitted.
#' - SIG = Significant Discharge Facility
#' - NONSIG = Nonsignificant Discharge Facility
#' @param p_spcc SPCC/FRP Flag. A Y value limits results to facilities subject to SPCC/FRP to prevent and respond to oil spills.
#' @param p_st Facility State and State-Equivalent Filter.  Provide one or more USPS postal abbreviations for states and state-equivalents to filter results.  Provide multiple values as a comma-delimited list.
#' @param p_start_date Monitoring Period Start Date. Provide a date value in MM/YYYY format to specify the first monitoring period to include in results. Parameter p_end_date must also be populated when using this parameter.
#' @param p_tmdl Chesapeake Bay TMDL Flag. A Y value will limit results to facilities that contribute to the Chesapeake Bay TMDL.
#' @param p_watershed Watershed. Provide a watershed name in combination with p_watershed_group to restrict results.
#' @param p_watershed_group Major U.S. Watershed. Provide one of the following codes to restrict results. 
#' - M = Major Watersheds
#' - U = USGS Watersheds
#' - L = Large Aquatic Ecosystems Program
#' - N = National Estuaries Program
#' @param p_year Required.  The calendar year for the DMR annual pollutant loadings. The year must be 2007 or later.
#' @param p_zip 5-Digit ZIP Code Filter. Provide one or more 5-digit postal zip codes to filter results.  May contain multiple comma-separated values.
#' @param p_fac_ico FRS tribal land code flag. Enter Y or N to include or exclude facilities based on a FRS tribal land code.
#' @param p_ico Indian Country Flag.  Enter a Y or N to restrict searches to facilities inside or outside Indian Country.
#' @param p_icoo Indian country search and/or flag. Enter Y to set Indian country search conditions to return any results found using p_ico, p_fac_ico or p_fac_icoo. Otherwise only results matching all provided p_ico, p_fac_ico or p_fac_icoo conditions will be returned.
#' @param p_pctlowinc Percent Low Income filter. Enter a value to restrict results to facilities with a given percentage of low income population within a 3-mile radius.
#' @param p_pm Percent People of Color Limiter. Enter a value to restrict results to facilities with a given percentage of people of color within a 3-mile radius.
#' 
#' NONE = 0\%
#' GTx = greater than x\%
#' GTEx = greater than or equal to x\%
#' @param p_tribedist Proximity to tribal land limiter. Enter a value of mile(s) between 0 and 25 to filter results. This parameter is only evaluated if p_tribeid is populated.
#' @param p_tribeid Numeric code for tribe (or list of tribes).
#' @param pageno Indicates the number of the page to display. It is used only when the results are paginated.
#' @param newsort Output Sort Column.  Enter the number of the column on which the data will be sorted. If unpopulated results will sort on the first column.
#' @param descending Output Sort Column Descending Flag.  Enter Y to column identified in the newsort parameter descending.  Enter N to use ascending sort order. Used only when newsort parameter is populated.
#' @param responseset Response Set Limiter. Enter a value to limit the number of records per page. Value cannot exceed 1,000.
#' @param callback JSONP Callback.  For use with JSONP and GEOJSONP output only.  Enter a name of the function in which to wrap the JSON response.
#' @param qcolumns Used to customize service output.  A list of comma-separated column IDs of output objects that will be returned in the service query object or download.  Use the metadata service endpoint for a complete list of Ids and definitions.
#' @param suppress_headers Suppress Headers. A Y value will suppress download title and search criteria from being included in CSV output. Column headers will still be provided.
#' @return Decoded response returned by the client request helper.
